## 1. Objective
Currently, `src/components/CodeEditor.tsx` scrolls the code editor during playback using `editor.revealLineInCenterIfOutsideViewport?.(Math.max(1, mRange.startLine - 2), 0)`. Because `revealLineInCenterIfOutsideViewport` only scrolls when the line has completely exited the visible screen, the active measure drifts down to the bottom edge of the editor before jumping, and using `mRange.startLine - 2` targets the top of the measure rather than its vertical center. This contract introduces `computeActiveMeasureScrollTarget()` in `src/components/CodeEditor.tsx` and switches playback scrolling to `editor.revealLinesInCenter(startLine, endLine, 0)` and `editor.revealLineInCenter(centerLine, 0)` so the current `measure N { ... }` block is **always kept in the exact vertical center** of the code editor as playback progresses, while bumping the repository version from `5.0.6` to `5.0.8` and updating `README.md`.

